-- `syntax!`: a parser and a lossless tree, written from an ungrammar.
--
--   syntax! {
--     pub Calc
--     lexer Token
--     trivia { Whitespace, Comment }
--     tokens {
--       "let" = Let, "ident" = Ident _, "self" as SelfWord = Ident "self", …
--     }
--     context { "label" = Ident _ before Colon, … }
--     precedence Expr { left "+" "-", left "*" "/", postfix Call }
--     grammar {
--       File = Stmt*
--       …
--     }
--   }
--
-- writes, beside the call:
--
-- * `Calc`, every kind of node and token the tree can hold;
-- * a parse function for each rule, emitting events over `Lingua.Parser`;
-- * `parseCalc : String -> (Green Calc, [(Int, String)])`, which lexes with
--   the Scythe lexer `lexToken`, parses, and builds the lossless tree;
-- * the typed AST: `CalcLet`, `asCalcLet`, `calcLetName`, … -- everything
--   named after `Calc` (see "names" below).
--
-- A token's kind is its constructor's, `Ident _`'s `Ident` -- or, for an entry
-- whose pattern says what the token's text is, `Ident "self"`, a kind of its
-- own, tried first: named `as`, or after the quoted name. And some kinds a
-- token has only where it is, which no fixed number of tokens ahead could
-- tell the parser: `context` says them, each a pattern and where the token
-- has to be -- `before` a token, `after` one, or on a path of tokens, `a.b.c`,
-- `ending` in one, `via` the one between them:
--
--   context {
--     "mac_lower" = LowerIdent _ ending Bang via Period,
--     "pattern" = LowerIdent "pattern" before UpperIdent _
--   }
--
-- The first that holds of a token gives it its kind, and a token none holds
-- of keeps the table's. Neighbours are the tokens either side that are not
-- trivia.
--
-- See docs/DESIGN.md for what each rule becomes. Every mistake is reported
-- where it was written: in the tables, at the token; in the grammar, at the
-- byte inside the string.

